# The fixture corpus is raw binary, and must survive checkout untouched.
#
# Without this, git on Windows applies `core.autocrlf` and rewrites every 0x0A byte in a `.bin`
# file as 0x0D 0x0A. That is not a subtle corruption: the first CI run on Windows read a 5x5
# Float32 kernel as 125 bytes instead of 100 — 25 of its bytes happened to be 0x0A — and the
# fixture loader rejected it. Every fixture-backed assertion in the suite, including the OpenCV
# comparison that is the package's correctness gate, depends on these bytes being exact.
#
# `-text` marks a path as never subject to end-of-line conversion, in either direction.
*.bin -text

# The wisdom file is FFTW's own serialisation format, written and read through C `fopen`/`fclose`.
# Not currently committed, but the same rule must apply if one ever is.
*.wisdom -text

# Text files that must keep LF regardless of platform, because tools other than git read them.
*.jl text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
